From a701c5cc5d4413f6475b1a22973251897396035c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:13:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 43/51] coh 76: keep only what the v6 figures use; TLS without
 init wrappers; RwLock fast path inlined

- MEGALON_COH_DETAIL=1 (default off) gates what no v6 figure needs:
  switch_rw / reclaim counts and times (parts of write start), KV create
  counts/ns and KV shares (reserved[3..6]), the NR object replay-flush
  statistics (process-wide atomics in exec_notify, port-added).
- Sections reach their coh::Tls through ThreadLocalMeta (set at Register);
  coh::tls is constinit (no TLS init wrapper calls); object counters hang off
  the Tls.
- RwLock::read: the uncontended first iteration inlined, the waiting loop
  (with the wait accounting) out of line; same algorithm as upstream.
- Timed anchors read the TSC without the section gate (no thread-local read
  inside the measured lookup); one shared execute_anchor copy.
- NR/object tests enable the replay-flush statistics they check.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
